<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hannibal Mago</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 406 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a> · Also known as Hannibal son of Gisco</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a> Mago was a Carthaginian general of the Magonid family, grandson of the Hamilcar who had died at the Battle of Himera in 480 BCE. In 409 BCE he led a large army to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>, where he stormed Selinous and then destroyed Himera, reportedly executing 3,000 prisoners to avenge his grandfather. He returned in 406 BCE to besiege Akragas but died of plague during the siege.</p></div>
